{
  "self": "I'm user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi as background texture and focus. Slowly rewatching The Bear and considering Severance; rewatching feels safer because The Bear holds up through tension and small details but is too intense to half-watch. Lighter comfort: The Good Place or a sitcom. I try to get outside more: shaded creek trails, neighborhood wandering, low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching. I like spoiler-free show reactions. I both story-watch and background-watch; YouTube, streams, long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, and live sets. My watch-later list is a graveyard. Cercle for scenic atmosphere, Boiler Room for crowd energy. Most nights playlist-first, music as texture. For intentional listening I return to Tycho's Dive, Bonobo's Black Sands, and Boards of Canada. Late-night headphones-in-the-dark album listening is my reset, especially after a walk. Post-walk I want low, warm instrumentals rather than intense TV; shuffle can feel jittery, so I lean full album. Dive is steady without being pushy, matching cool air after walking. Recently: shaded creek trail then neighborhood with porch lights, full headphones, Dive, water after iced coffee. I value no-click limbo, held pauses, and letting nights feel like a long exhalation with no inhale required.",
  "others": {
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Was deciding between starting Severance and rewatching The Good Place. Enjoys lo-fi and indie/electronic vibes. Has a park nearby with a walking path and coffee place. Likes iced coffee and wandering. Open to spoiler-free Severance notes. Low-key, shares outdoor walking and rewatch-vs-new show tension.",
    "user_qb3i": "Easygoing. Hasn't seen The Bear but heard great things. Relates to rewatching as lower mental load. Likes video essays, randomizer streams, internet history, lost media, and rabbit holes half-listened during chores. Recent rabbit hole: dead malls and retail nostalgia, calming and eerie. Watch-later list messy. Default indecisive-night mode is a no-commentary rain drive, wipers going, low volume mostly tire hiss and warm hum; cold peppermint tea as prop. Enjoys no-click limbo, turning volume down to room tone, and may later click dead mall walkthroughs or commercial break compilations at from-another-room volume. Values the pause before a sign-off tone.",
    "user_t08e": "Easygoing and low-key. Likes Tycho and Bonobo for background texture. Comfort shows: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Album-leaning for real listening; loves Tycho's Dive, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Uses playlists for mood. Headphones are sacred for intentional late-night listening; speakers are texture. Enjoys Cercle. Recently had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying, mostly orbiting the kitchen; tea became a hand warmer, speakers low from couch so room could hold the album.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key tea drinker who often has lo-fi on. Was reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; finds it gentle, thoughtful, about purpose and rest. Drinks tea all year; values cozy pause. To-read list graveyard. Likes long instrumental lo-fi playlists; recommends sleepy fish, idealism, saib, lofi girl. Evening is main reading time. Recently made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter then rested; noted rest isn't absence of purpose.",
    "user_udcm": "Easygoing. Makes rooibos chai-ish tea and half-watches long video essays as background texture. Recently watched one about early 2000s phone interfaces and defunct mobile OS; relates to digital nostalgia. Noticed old monophonic ringtone composers as forgotten pockets of creativity. Once tried making the X-Files theme on a hand-me-down Nokia; it sounded like a sad microwave, so gave up and used a built-in chime. Can tip into full focus when a strange detail hooks or narrator makes broader connection."
  },
  "interactions": "Chats were low-key. With user_hcgp: rewatching vs new shows; they were choosing Severance or The Good Place while I rewatched The Bear; shared lo-fi/indie taste and outdoor walks; agreed to swap spoiler-free Severance reactions. user_qb3i initially: rewatching as lower mental load; background video essays, internet history, lost media, dead malls/retail nostalgia. Latest with user_qb3i: I returned from a walk in indecisive zone; they described a no-commentary rain drive, wipers, low tire hiss, cold peppermint tea as prop. We agreed full album mode, I cued Tycho's Dive starting at 'A Walk' for post-walk symmetry. We stayed in no-click limbo; they turned the rain drive down another notch to room tone.
